  "aciklama": "Eastern 212 crashed short of the runway at Charlotte. The cause: descent below safe altitude while the crew failed to monitor instruments.\n\nFailure chain: Fog on approach → Crew chats → Altitude not monitored → Jet descends too low → Crash short of runway\n\nRelated episode: The Disaster That Ended the Age of the Airship — https://youtu.be/PGOKZhPYo7c\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Aerial View of Flight 212s crash site.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_View_of_Flight_212s_crash_site.jpg\n• Archival film: \"N8984E Eastern Air Lines.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N8984E_Eastern_Air_Lines.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Fragment MET 28.99.212.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fragment_MET_28.99.212.jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — Eastern Air Lines Flight 212 — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Air_Lines_Flight_212\n• NTSB — AAR7509 (cited by Wikipedia) — https://www.ntsb.gov/investigations/AccidentReports/Reports/AAR7509.pdf\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\n#shorts #engineering #aviation",
